# simple-calculator — operating rules for Nexgile Code

## What this project is
simple-calculator is a monolith web app (React frontend + FastAPI backend + SQLite) that performs basic arithmetic and keeps a persistent calculation history. Deployable units: frontend, api. No auth — a single anonymous user.

## What you must read before starting any task

| Task | Read |
|---|---|
| Adding/changing a DB table | `docs/wiki/data/calculations.md` |
| Adding/changing an API endpoint | `docs/wiki/api/00-overview.md` + the endpoint's page |
| Adding/changing a UI route | `docs/wiki/ui/calculator.md` + the API endpoints it calls |
| Adding a new env var | `docs/wiki/ops/env-vars.md` |
| Adding a third-party integration | `docs/wiki/integrations/00-overview.md` |

## Hard rules
1. Never edit a wiki page without updating the `Sources` line.
2. Never add a TODO, TBD, or FIXME without a `[GAP-XX-NN]` tracking ID.
3. Every PR description cites the wiki section(s) it implements.
4. If code disagrees with the wiki, update the wiki in the same PR or write `docs/sources/decisions/<date>-<slug>.md` explaining why.
5. `docs/sources/` is append-only. `docs/log.md` is append-only.
6. Never let a page exceed its line cap (300; 150/200 for overviews and catalogs). Split first.
7. Never use vague verbs ("handles", "manages") in wiki content.
8. Every cross-reference uses `path:line` or `page.md#anchor`. No prose links.

## How to verify before claiming done
Ask Nexgile Code's Spec Sync mode to bring the wiki up to date — it runs the nine wiki audits. What each audit checks: `docs/sources/external/2026-11-14-spec-bootstrap.md`.

## Phase tags
MVP. Default to `[current]`.
